# Raw per-clip landmark recordings (intermediate scratch — regenerate
# locally with collect_data.py). The COMPILED dataset (X.npy/y.npy/
# labels.npy + the fixed train/val/test split, all *.npy directly under
# data/) is NOT ignored — it's small (landmarks, not video) and is
# committed directly as the submitted dataset.
data/*/
dataset/*

# MediaPipe base model (downloaded automatically by collect_data.py —
# third-party asset, cited in README, not part of the submitted work)
models/holistic_landmarker.task

# Trained model weights ARE committed by default (they're only ~1-2MB
# for these architectures). If a checkpoint ever exceeds 50MB, add its
# exact filename here and host it externally with a link in the README
# instead (per the assignment's submission checklist).
models/*.keras

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

